Download a registered evaluator version's definition.

Usage
  azd ai eval evaluator download <name> [flags]

Flags
      --force                   : Overwrite a file that already exists.
      --output-dir string       : Directory to write into. Defaults to the current directory.
      --output-file string      : Exact path to write.
      --project-endpoint string : Foundry project endpoint.
      --version string          : Version to download. Omit for the latest, which is reported.

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for download
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
  Download the latest rubric to a local file
    azd ai eval evaluator download my-rubric --output-file rubric.json
